Car Price Prediction is a machine learning project that aims to predict the selling price of a car based on different features of the vehicle. 
The main purpose of this project is to understand how factors such as the car’s brand, age, engine size, fuel type, transmission, mileage, condition,
and model can affect its price.In this task, we worked with a car price dataset containing information about different cars. 
The dataset included features such as Car ID, Brand, Year, Engine Size, Fuel Type, Transmission, Mileage, Condition, Price, and Model.
First, the dataset was loaded and explored using Python and pandas. We checked the columns and data to understand what information was available.
The data was then prepared for machine learning by handling the different types of values and converting the required information into a format
that the model could understand.
Next, we analysed the relationship between the car features and their prices. Data visualization was used to understand patterns in the dataset.
Graphs helped us see how factors such as the year, mileage, engine size, and other characteristics can influence the price of a car.
After preparing the data, a machine learning model was trained using the available car features. 
The model learned patterns from the existing data and used those patterns to estimate the price of a car.
The model's predictions were then compared with the actual prices to understand how well it performed.
The project demonstrates how machine learning can be used in the automobile industry to estimate vehicle prices.
Such a system can help sellers set reasonable prices and help buyers understand the expected value of a vehicle.
